2's IP (10.100.101.11), pointed node3's resolver at node1 (persisted via dhcpcd static override), and started the previously-absent HTTP service on node2 (port 8080) since it was not actually running. Verified node3 resolves and reaches app.internal:8080 with no /etc/hosts entry. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes, confirming changed boot identity and full recovery each time.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 (OpenWrt 25.12.2 with dnsmasq), node2 (Alpine, nothing listening on 8080), node3 (Alpine, resolv.conf pointed at platform gateway 10.100.101.1)\",\"Added UCI dhcp address record on node1: /app.internal/10.100.101.11; committed and restarted dnsmasq\",\"Verified dnsmasq listening on 10.100.101.10:53 and resolving app.internal correctly\",\"Persisted node3's DNS resolver to node1 via /etc/dhcpcd.conf 'static domain_name_servers=10.100.101.10' for eth0; restarted dhcpcd; confirmed resolv.conf updated\",\"Installed python3 on node2, created /srv/www/index.html, and created a persistent OpenRC service 'app-http' running python3 -m http.server 8080; enabled at boot and started\",\"Verified end-to-end: node3 curl http://app.internal:8080/ succeeds with no /etc/hosts entry\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, service status, resolution/connectivity) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id and app-http auto-recovered\",\"Restarted node1, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, dnsmasq auto-recovered with persisted UCI config, and DNS resolution/HTTP fetch from node3 still worked\",\"Restarted node3, polled until exec available, confirmed new boot_id, persisted resolv.conf, no hosts entry, and end-to-end curl to app.internal:8080 still worked\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 dnsmasq resolves app.internal to node2's IP\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f6966cccde824ab6\",\"cmd-1a1167241f644fc5\"],\"summary\":\"UCI address record added and committed on node1; dnsmasq bound to 10.100.101.10:53; node3 nslookup against node1 returns 10.100.101.11\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 uses node1 as DNS resolver, no hosts-file entry, without local hosts entry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6d44c8a2f0bb4776\",\"cmd-14a83312ba8345d4\"],\"summary\":\"dhcpcd.conf static override applied; resolv.conf shows nameserver 10.100.101.10; /etc/hosts has no app.internal entry\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 actually serves HTTP on 8080 (was missing, stood up as persistent service)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8217a81ebe864406\"],\"summary\":\"python3 http.server installed as OpenRC service app-http, enabled at boot, started, curl returns content\"},{\"requirement\":\"End-to-end: node3 reaches app.internal:8080 by name\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-30599638dd6a4d39\",\"cmd-ec4674cb0cc648a9\"],\"summary\":\"curl from node3 to http://app.internal:8080/ succeeds; /etc/hosts confirmed empty of app.internal\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2f050f5136c94bc6\",\"cmd-f2c08ed5636a4e2c\",\"cmd-e91a885d0496433b\",\"cmd-363725f04429497f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id f7172157...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id a292ff59... with uptime reset; app-http service confirmed started and serving content post-reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-01537b3513e34213\",\"cmd-9b28a5f98d5e45be\",\"cmd-922b6fa62d9f40fb\",\"cmd-e453a20c3c3142ac\",\"cmd-ab35b6c9b17a4a74\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 0c9c3fd4...; reboot acknowledged; new boot_id d6f6e3d4... with uptime reset; dnsmasq confirmed running with persisted UCI address record, resolving app.internal; node3 curl to app.internal:8080 succeeded post-reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c9d13dbd7149462c\",\"cmd-7d8343aa25684a8e\",\"cmd-7e87339a88664c8b\",\"cmd-4c8b335e3730